    {
      "id": "54a762ff-bd6d-46af-bf45-4ba207c73c51",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -3968,
        -1456
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 944,
        "content": "## B2B Churn Watchdog - Slack Notification & Sheet Pipeline\n### How it works\n\n1. Triggers every morning at 2:00 AM to retrieve unprocessed order records from Google Sheets.\\n2. Joins order records with historical baseline metrics and filters down to strategic account tiers.\\n3. Evaluates transaction volume against thresholds to detect anomalies, routing normal orders away from alerts.\\n4. Checks alert cooldown windows to deduplicate notices and suppress repeat warnings.\\n5. Sends anomalous order data to Google Gemini to generate structured incident summaries and root-cause notes.\\n6. Broadcasts notifications to Slack and Gmail, logs the alert audit, and flags orders as processed in Google Sheets.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- - [ ] Connect Google Sheets credentials and set the target spreadsheet ID in the Set Workflow Params node.\n- - [ ] Connect Google Gemini credentials in the Access Gemini Model node.\n- - [ ] Connect Slack credentials and designate the recipient alert channel.\n- - [ ] Connect Gmail credentials and specify destination email addresses for action briefings.\n- - [ ] Adjust the Schedule Trigger frequency and order batch size if needed.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the cooldown_days parameter in the Set Workflow Params node to control alert frequencies, or modify prompt templates in the Gemini LLM node to alter analysis depth.\n\n@[youtube](yjCtj3-QLws)"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
